From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arian <arian.kulmer@web.de>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:55:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix slow-motion frame selection and codec image layout

Decode all compressed samples before selecting frames for slow motion.
Skipping samples before decoding loses reference pictures with inter-frame
recordings and causes stale pixels and motion trails. Select decoded
outputs instead, preserving the transition into the interpolated segment.

Copy YUV data through codec Image planes, respecting crop, row stride and
pixel stride. The interpolator expects packed NV12, while codec images may
be planar or have padded luma/chroma planes, including a 736-line slice
height for 720p on zeus.

Assisted-by: LLM
